Verification: a real format-1 RocksDB checkpoint image is opened through `RocksDB.openReadOnly`. The physical inspector enforces finite file/byte bounds, exact column-family inventory, empty default column family with checked iterator status, manifest file length/checksum equality, and exact Store format/Shard/db identity/incarnation, checkpoint ID, applied source position, and mutation sequence. The state inventory scans every registered Column Family under finite record/byte/time bounds; it counts key-kind prefixes, decodes old Message status and retired identity records, and checks each Message key/source route belongs to the checkpoint Shard. For typed SCHEDULED records it rebuilds and verifies the due/ordered key from Message and source fields, then checks the persisted DUE/ORDERED and EXPIRY values. It reports conservative per-Message disposition counts and stable blockers for claimed, SCHEDULED messages with open Attempt obligations, unresolved send, handoff and terminal states. Missing indexes return a stable conflict bound to the old Message key digest and canonical source position. The manifest-bound physical inventory is checked before and after the logical scan. Tests cover valid indexes, a missing expiry-index conflict, malformed Message rejection without file changes, read-budget exhaustion, a SCHEDULED uncertain retry blocked by its open Attempt obligation, conservative disposition mapping, and a manifest/image mismatch.

